{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/447922-play-by-post-the-eternal-world-of-darkness","id":447922,"title":"[Play by Post] The Eternal World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-18T10:31:40-07:00","id":447922,"title":"[Play by Post] The Eternal World of Darkness","content":"Alright, it's about time I start a campaign and stick to it, and so I decided to do a multi-gameline Classic World of Darkness chronicle that is metaplot-free and decidedly NOT Gothic-Punk. A game more like 1e and 2e cWoD and nothing at all like the material found in Revised. I had tossed this idea around before many times, but never really did anything with it. This is basically my dream game and I will need both players and maybe a few assistant ST's to help with Werewolf and Changeling, as I am not very familiar with those gamelines. However, I can handle Vampire, Mortals, Senshi, and maybe Mage (I might need help with Mage, depending on how many people are interested in it, as I have never actually ran Mage, but I do own the 2e corebook). Essentially I want to run my dream campaign.<br /> <br /> <br /> The setting is somewhat different from the canon cWoD. I'm sure some of you know of these differences between my WoD and the official WoD, but for those who don't know, here's a run-down.<br /> <br /> The biggest difference is the total lack of metaplot. It's not metaplot-agnostic but completely metaplot-free. Gangrel are still in the Camarilla, Ravnos are a full clan, Stargazers are still in the Garou Nation, Malkavians still have Dominate, Tremere Antitribbu are still around, and there was no Avatar Storm, Red Star, Sixth Great Maelstrom, or any other apocalyptic Revised Edition shenanigans. Nothing wrong with those Revised metaplot things per se, I just don't like them and don't want them in my games.<br /> <br /> Also, the gamelines <i>Kindred of the East, </i><i>Hunter: The Reckoning, </i>and <i>Demon: The Fallen </i>don't exist in this iteration of the Classic World of Darkness. At all. No Fallen, no Kuei-Jin, no Imbued. East Asia's cities are dominated by Cainites (though not necessarily the Camarilla and Sabbat), and the Judeo-Christian creation myth is no longer objectively true (The whole Caine myth is just a theory that was predominant among Western Kindred back in the day. Who knows if it's actually Caine who was the first vampire?)<br /> <br /> Overall, the chronicle eschews Gothic and Punk aesthetics and mindsets in exchange for something more anime-influenced along with some heavy metal influences on the side. In terms of mindset, it's more like Iron Maiden and Judas Priest, less like Sisters of Mercy and The Cure.<br /> <br /> Golconda is very much a possibility, and once a vampire achieves Golconda, they become human again. However, it is very hard to achieve. We're trying to be more like 1st Edition Masquerade, which in my opinion, was a game of salvation and redemption (the good kind of personal horror in my opinion), instead of damnation and apocalypticism like Revised Edition (which isn't really my cup of tea).<br /> <br /> Now that I have repeated that stuff for the umpteenth time, onto the actual ideas behind the game.<br /> <br /> That being said, the gamelines <i>Vampire: The Masquerade, Werewolf: The Apocalypse, Mage: The Ascension, Wraith: The Oblivion, Changeling: The Dreaming, Laws of the Hunt, </i>and the fan-game <i>Senshi: The Merchandising </i>are fully in play. I may or may not include <i>Street Fighter: The Storytelling Game </i>as an option since I like the game and never got to play it, but I am not sure of that.<br /> <br /> The setting is still yet to be determined, I am unsure if I should use Chicago (with Lodin still Prince, and all the memorable characters from Chicago By Night 1e present as NPC's), a New York City that was Camarilla and never controlled by the Sabbat ever, or a fictional city such as Empire Bay or Liberty City. The campaign would start out focused on Vampire, and piece-by-piece we'll bring in Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Mortals, and Senshi.<br /> <br /> Would anyone be interested in this type of chronicle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-18-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:05:44-07:00","id":449330,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind playing a mortal for something like this, even though I'm less familiar with CWoD. I'd rather play a mortal because I'm not a huge fan of vampires (in terms of playing them, I am actually a huge fan of vampire fiction) and I might be interested in Mage, but I'd rather not ask someone to learn it (I am trying to run Awakening right now, it's a bit tricky). I also like the idea of not being heavily tied to the metaplot and it being more open.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","user":"NovaP","date":". 03-19-2015, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","name":"NovaP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}